xt":"The new "},{"code":"ServerTrustPolicyManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since different servers and web services can have different leaf certificates, intermediate and even root"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"certficates, it is important to have the flexibility to specify evaluation policies on a per host basis. This","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allows for scenarios such as using default evaluation for host1, certificate pinning for host2, public key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pinning for host3 and disabling evaluation for host4."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/sunday\/servertrustpolicymanager\/init(policies:)"]}],"references":{"doc://Sunday/documentation/Sunday":{"title":"Sunday","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sunday\/documentation\/Sunday","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/sunday"},"doc://Sunday/documentation/Sunday/ServerTrustPolicy":{"url":"\/documentation\/sunday\/servertrustpolicy","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServerTrustPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" evaluates the server trust generally provided by an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSURLAuthenticationChallenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connecting to a server over a secure HTTPS connection. The policy configuration then evaluates the server trust"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a given set of criteria to determine whether the server trust is valid and the connection should be made."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sunday\/documentation\/Sunday\/ServerTrustPolicy","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"te